WEBVTT

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.330
<i>The first dialogue held between 
humanity and Yaha-kui zaShunina</i>

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.010
<i>was held in front of the media.</i>

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.940
<i>Yaha-kui zaShunina said that he was 
a visitor from outside the universe,</i>

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.950
<i>what he called "the anisotropic,"</i>

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:30.460
<i>and promised to release the 
passengers held within Kado.</i>

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.920
<i>Then, when Yaha-kui zaShunina was 
asked about the reason for his visit,</i>

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.480
<i>he showed humanity the anisotropic 
devices known as Wam.</i>

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.380
<i>These devices were beyond human technology,</i>

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.700
<i>and offered the promise of infinite energy.</i>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.160
Rotowa

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.320
Gonno-san?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.500
Gonno-san!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.480
Wake up.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.170
What day is today?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.570
The 29th.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.960
It's only been three days, huh?

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.080
You mean it's been <i>three whole days!</i>

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.190
There's too much to film, 
and not enough time.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.720
It's like a festival.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.440
A festival for humanity.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.660
At noon today, if Yaha-kui 
zaShunina's statement is correct,

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.160
two of the passengers from 
the plane will be released.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.680
The first two have been released!

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:33.520
We can see what appears to 
be a mother with her child!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.640
Yes!

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.100
If this continues to go 
as planned, in 25 days,

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.560
all 251 passengers will be released!

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:50.020
That's one big problem 
getting solved, huh?

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.740
There's a lot left to go,

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.010
but now that two passengers are out,
 it feels like we're making progress.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.150
He was accurate down to the second.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.650
Can we trust this "anisotropic being" guy?

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.710
Does that thing even have the concept of lying?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.970
That's...

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:15.090
Shindo!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.320
<b>Local Response Team Forward Base
for Large Cube That Appeared on 7/25</b>

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.650
My name is Asano. I'm an aide with

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.740
the Local Kado Response Team, working for 
the National Public Safety Committee.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:27.660
I'm Shindo, Ministry of Foreign 
Affairs, UN Policy Bureau.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.920
You idiot.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.170
Shindo.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.210
Ubuka-san.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.770
Well done.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.010
Now, we have a job for you.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.980
The government has given 
the official orders.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.600
Shindo Kojiro, official for the 
Ministry of Foreign Policy,

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.190
is excused from his current 
duties as of today,

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.820
and appointed as the special envoy from the 
Japanese government to the anisotropic.

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.960
Special envoy to the anisotropic?

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:04.780
We need the ability to make 
decisions at an unprecedented speed.

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:09.870
The special envoy is to be given 
equivalent decision-making powers

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:09.870
<b>Presently Released: 2/251 People</b>

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:14.360
to the prime minister in the national 
security, political, and economic fields.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.860
We need your abilities, Shindo.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.370
Let's make it Hanamori.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.020
I think it'll be harder to deal 
with anisotropic issues

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.050
with a Japanese government title.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.770
It would be easier to officially 
entrust these powers to Hanamori

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.600
and give me more freedom of movement.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.600
Then you're going to continue as the 
negotiator for the anisotropic side?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.310
Yes.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:45.940
There are talented people here.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.580
Yes, I understand.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:50.150
Things will be more balanced if 
I'm on the anisotropic side.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.910
All right, I'll confirm that.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:54.160
I guess it's weird for me to be part 
of the Foreign Affairs Ministry, too.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.970
Ubuka-san, can you fire me?

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.070
Got it.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:02.750
I'll throw in a severance package.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.200
Okay, Shindo-san, negotiator 
for the anisotropic side,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.900
I'd like you to get started by

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.210
meeting with the government immediately.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.760
<b>Prime Minister's Residence</b>

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.970
<b>First Anisotropic Problem Response Planning Meeting</b>

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.940
There are countless problems here,

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:20.040
but the Wam are the most pressing.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.720
No fuel is needed. They 
generate no pollution.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:26.850
A system capable of drawing 
infinite electricity from space.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.040
It's an energy tap that can be 
affixed anywhere in the world.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.280
Properly set up,

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:38.820
a single one of them could meet 
the entire world's energy supply.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.710
That's terrifying.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.630
Japan has presently been given 167 Wam.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.640
Yaha-kui zaShunina is still within Kado,

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.070
performing a process called transformation.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:56.600
He's taking out approximately ten 
Wam a day from the anisotropic.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:02.270
First, I want to hear what the Japanese 
government is planning for the Wam.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.770
The Unified Science Research Lab is presently

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:09.700
having a special team do 
a detailed investigation on it.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.050
First, we need to learn more 
about what the Wam is.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.990
I'd like to have access 
to that information, too.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.390
Can I see it later?

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:20.260
Yes.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.450
How are the people responding?

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:28.120
Public opinion is extremely confused 
as to how to deal with the Wam.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.640
Should we build good relations and 
enjoy the benefits of the Wam?

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:36.620
Should we try to remove Kado from 
Haneda Airport using military force?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.280
There are a lot of extreme 
opinions out there,

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:45.140
but the most common opinion is neutral:
 "I don't know," or "I can't say."

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.650
What about overseas?

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.720
The UN is presently holding 
a conference to discuss the Wam.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:55.620
<b>UN Security Council Meeting</b>

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:55.490
The permanent members of the security 
council have made their demands clear.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:02.740
Japan must give all Wam to the UN, 
and allow the UN to manage them.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.020
An infinite energy source brought 
from outside the universe...

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.760
Only allowing one country access to these

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:13.040
could destroy the world's 
socioeconomic power balance!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:18.510
The security council considers Japan's 
keeping the Wam to themselves a problem.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:23.100
Our information indicates that
they're considering sanctions.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.890
Sanctions!

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.660
Prime Minister, the security 
council has a point.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:34.520
If another country tried to monopolize the Wam,
Japan would make the same demands.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:39.340
Given the scale of their effect, don't you 
think the UN should control the Wam?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.250
What does the anisotropic believe?

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:46.280
Can you hold off on that?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:53.770
I'll confirm, but Yaha-kui zaShunina may not
wish to see them turned over to the UN.

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:55.290
The bread, huh?

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.030
I'll mostly be at Haneda for a while.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.190
Take care of things here.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.280
Just don't work too hard, okay?

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.180
That'll be the toughest 
thing for Shindo, huh?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:14.130
I'm just lucky I've been running on adrenaline 
for so long that I don't feel sleepy.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.400
Shindo-san, hurry up!

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:18.910
We've got a lot to do!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.160
I'm on my way!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.310
See you.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:26.330
This inspection was your idea.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.290
Sorry.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.980
Don't apologize, just do your job.

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:29.530
Okay, time to get to work.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.720
Please understand your position 
and your importance.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.840
I'm sorry.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:42.810
The situation is changing by the second!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.980
You need to understand 
exactly where we stand!

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.060
You and I are both representing our sides!

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.010
No, I mean, I'm one thing,

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.820
but you're the only representative 
for the anisotropic in the world.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:57.480
But you...

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.490
I thought we were short on time?

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.750
The results of the latest opinion survey.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.070
We should work with the UN and neighboring countries to deal with this. 
Yaha-kui zaShunina is hot. 
I live in the country, so I don't care. 
We should get closer to the anisotropic. 
We should get rid of Kado. 
We should drop a bomb on Kado.
I like things as they are. 
I want to use the Wam.
I love the patterns on the side of Kado.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.290
The Japanese government is too slow.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.290
A bomb on Kado?

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:12.440
It probably wouldn't work.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.310
What's your opinion, Tsukai-san?

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:18.040
As someone who spoke with him directly,

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:22.390
I'd like to hear your honest 
feelings on the anisotropic being.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.020
My impression was that Yaha-kui zaShunina

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.470
didn't seem to consider humanity his enemy.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.880
It's unknown if he even possesses 
the concepts of good and evil.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.680
But for now, there seems to be
little intention to harm us.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.500
However, even if he has no 
evil intentions of his own,

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.320
it's too early for humanity 
to have the Wam.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:46.840
It's a wonderful thing, yes,

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.620
but used wrong, it could be a disaster.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:55.220
I think we're better off without the Wam.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.580
Even though it's a source 
of infinite energy?

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:00.460
Yes.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:05.770
I thought the only ones who were purely 
against it were the oil-producing countries.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:07.220
Why?

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.590
There are various opinions.

00:11:14.550 --> 00:11:16.340
By the way, Tsukai-san...

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.740
What?

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.040
At the meeting three days ago...

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:20.950
Yes.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.360
You burst out laughing, didn't you?

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.670
I did not.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.830
You did.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.210
I did not.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:34.390
I have video.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.820
<i>Discord. Friction—</i>

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.960
<i>Fregonics is fine.</i>

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:43.970
Nervousness and Relaxation

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.850
<i>Fregonics is fine.</i>

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:45.010
What is this?!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.880
It was broadcast all over the country.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:48.720
Delete it! I'm sending a delete request!

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:49.910
Why were you laughing?

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:54.580
It was because you were talking to the 
anisotropic being like he was normal!

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:55.740
It was funny!

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:56.840
Is that funny?

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.160
It is!

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:59.610
There's something funny about you!

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:20.010
<b>National Institute for Integrated Sciences</b>

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.680
<b>Temporary Wam Research and Analysis Unit</b>

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:28.330
The Wam consists of two objects 
linked in some fashion.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:32.490
One functions as the positive pole, 
and the other as the negative.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:35.910
Touch an electrode to both and 
it will begin to conduct.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.040
It's very strange.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.950
The appropriate voltage is emitted 
depending on the circuit.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.980
So it's not a consistently high voltage?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:49.070
You can use it to replace a battery 
or an entire power plant.

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.820
I have no idea how it works.

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.110
What's it composed of?

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:54.450
Macromolecules.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:58.740
The closest equivalents we 
have are conductive plastics.

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:00.840
But the shape's the big thing...

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.760
The shape?

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.840
I used the NMR in Yokohama 
to look at one of them.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.850
It comes up with six measurement results.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.050
What does that mean?

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:12.960
Just what I said.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.670
It looks like one object, 
but it has six shapes.

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.690
I don't understand.

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:20.180
Me, neither.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:23.070
I hope I understand it before I die.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.490
<b>Mifune Lab</b>

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:30.860
A huge amount of Wam would eliminate 
the need for an electrical infrastructure.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.860
What about environmental 
problems or safety issues?

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:38.690
First, Wam emit no CO2.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.040
They're clean energy.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:43.550
But since they generate energy infinitely,

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:47.220
they will disrupt the atmosphere's 
heat supply and absorption balance.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:53.310
So too much use of Wam could contribute
to global warming in the future?

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:56.070
Anything's bad for you if used in excess.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.240
In the end, it's up to humanity.

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:03.060
Doctor, I'm borrowing this!

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.090
zaShunina!

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.230
Shindo-san!

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.080
Good to see you.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.170
Welcome back.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.440
Hello again.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.300
Where is he?

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:49.030
Over there.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.870
Hey, zaShunina!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.120
Welcome back, Shindo.

00:14:58.280 --> 00:14:59.820
Here's your dinner.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:03.540
Hey, can't you scan books directly?

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.540
<b>Dinosaur Encyclopedia</b>

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:04.920
I can.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.340
I just need to control 
the ink on the surface.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.340
Then why do you read them with your eyes?

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.760
Because that's the format 
they were made for.

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.180
I am simultaneously taking in the method, 
the speed, and the environment

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.350
for acquiring information.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.040
I see.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:21.340
Dinnertime!

00:15:25.740 --> 00:15:27.410
What about supplies?

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:31.070
We have the bare minimum of 
supplies we need for survival.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:34.480
So if we could get some entertainment, too,

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:37.880
something for kids and something for adults...

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:41.860
To be honest, it's mentally draining in here.

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:43.710
I want books, too.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.230
Go to a bookstore yourself.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.250
A bookstore?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.580
No, never mind.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.620
I'll bring you some.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.980
If you're not going to eat your yogurt, 
give it to me, Shindo-san.

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.980
How goes the passenger release?

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.150
As of now, five have left Kado.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:05.350
Excluding you, there are 246 left to go.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.720
Hanamori, I have instructions for you.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:13.780
As of today, you've been designated the 
Japanese government envoy to the anisotropic.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.110
What's that?

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:21.360
You'll be given massive powers in certain 
fields, rivaling the prime minister's.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.640
Not you?

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:25.620
No, it's you.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:29.430
Don't be crazy! Rivaling the prime minister?

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.440
That would mean I rivaled 
the prime minister, right?!

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:32.930
I can't do it! Nuh-uh, no way!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:35.220
Why do you always do the 
craziest stuff, Shindo-san?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.170
I can't...

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.960
<b>Gentle on the Stomach</b>

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:38.960
<b>Yogurt</b>

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:38.960
do it.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:40.670
Hanamori.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:45.100
I think you can do it.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.540
Shindo-san...

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:55.070
And so, this is now officially under 
the jurisdiction of the government.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.900
<b>Kado Release Order</b>

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.450
<b>Hanamori Shun</b>

00:16:57.110 --> 00:16:58.300
Why...

00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.900
Why...

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:02.960
Why am I last?

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.100
Why, Shindo-san?!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:07.950
Why do I have to be last?!

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.950
Shut up, special envoy!

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.030
Take better care of your envoys!

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:12.410
What is this?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.970
Request Document 

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:14.940
International negotiations.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.270
Human society's largest 
international organization,

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:24.360
the United Nations, has asked that 
all Wam be turned over to them.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.550
I want to know the anisotropic's 
opinion on this.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:31.280
If the Wam are given to the United Nations,

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.650
will they then be spread 
throughout all humanity?

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:36.710
Probably not.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:38.290
Why?

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:40.960
Because the interests of 
each country are different.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:42.620
Some want the Wam.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.940
Some will be damaged by them.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.940
These interests are colliding 
at the United Nations.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:53.700
The five permanent members of the UN 
Security Council will probably win in the end.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:56.170
What are the demands of 
those five countries?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.840
The same as nuclear weapons.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.580
Nonproliferation and strict control.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.500
I know.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.270
That's exactly the opposite 
of what you want.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.450
Shindo,

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.790
over the past several days,

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.870
I have observed the things called 
"countries" and learned.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:14.000
Countries?

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:20.130
They function well as a device 
for unifying the people's will.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:25.950
They are also an appropriate method for 
functioning as a shelter to protect

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:27.830
human groups inside a geographic area.

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:33.430
In terms of maintaining societal safety, 
they are a highly advanced community.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:38.960
But the idea has power 
beyond its definitions.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.580
You could say it's out of control.

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:45.880
Countries are out of control?

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.110
Countries do not eat bread.

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.830
The Wam are not gifts to countries.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:56.020
They are gifts to humanity.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:02.930
But you can't exactly give people
six billion Wam, can you?

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:07.280
Given the speed you're creating 
them at now, that's not realistic.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:11.780
There is another way to 
promote the spread of Wam.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:16.480
But for that, I need further cooperation 
from the Japanese government,

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.970
and their resolve.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.680
Resolve?

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.390
The resolve...

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.360
to drop a bomb on this world.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:35.140
Please give your votes, then.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:50.530
Inuzuka-san!

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.380
Shindo!

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:59.460
Early this morning, the UN Security 
Council passed resolution 2246.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:03.990
They're demanding the unconditional 
surrender of all Wam in Japan's possession

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.930
to the United Nations.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:11.190
Article Seven of the UN Charter will 
be applied if we fail to comply.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:13.690
Article Seven... "Actions to force compliance."

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:15.470
Financial restrictions,

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:16.660
travel prohibitions,

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.700
ending diplomatic resolution, and...

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.810
international military action.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.260
If the Wam are given to the UN,

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.940
the permanent members of the security 
council will decide what's done with them.

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:35.840
They'll attempt to keep them from 
proliferating due to the danger they pose.

00:20:36.990 --> 00:20:39.920
Humanity can't even handle nuclear weapons.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:45.250
Even with the infinite energy offered by Wam, 
this pessimistic decision is the best we can do?

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:50.300
Yaha-kui zaShunina told 
us to share the bread!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:52.910
That may be the ideal,

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:56.240
but realistically, on our own...

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:58.560
We can't overturn a UN 
security council decision!

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:03.450
Prime Minister, Yaha-kui zaShunina
 has a way around this.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:04.790
Really?

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:11.800
However, it requires the resolve of 
Japan as well as you, Prime Minister.

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:34.560
Hello?

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:37.810
zaShunina, I want to discuss 
this matter with you.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.430
I predicted this.

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:41.580
I have no issues here.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:43.560
<i>You said you need people.</i>

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:45.340
<i>Do you have a way to get them?</i>

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:49.160
I have already found a person 
who seems to fit the criteria.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.320
Our first candidate is...

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.240
We're with the Cabinet Intelligence 
and Research Office.

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:56.410
Can you come with us immediately?

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:58.660
Doctor?

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:00.660
Dr. Shinawa Kanata?

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:03.610
Me?

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.510
Wam should be given to humanity,

00:23:38.510 --> 00:23:40.430
and spread to all of them.

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:40.880
Huh?

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:45.030
I didn't understand anything...

00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:47.650
We've confirmed the launch 
of a carrier strike force.

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:49.810
So it includes sanctions, huh?

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:50.190
Nanoka
